  "gaps_restored": 26,
  "gaps_unrestorable": 34,
  "restoration_note": "This teaching describes the Father of Greatness through three nested structures: (1) his five members of light = the canonical five faculties (mind, thought, teaching, counsel, reflection); (2) his twelve members of light = the twelve wisdoms; (3) within each, the same fivefold completeness reiterated. Then a list of five attributes that gush forth: Light (first), Fragrance (second), Voice (third), [Greatness/operative power] (fourth), and Revelation-of-the-hidden (fifth). Sections 1207-1222 are well-preserved enough to confirm the editor's structural restorations (the canonical five faculties, the ordinal sequence ⲧϣⲁⲣⲓⲧ/ⲧⲙⲁⲥⲥⲛⲧⲉ/ⲧⲙⲁⲥϣⲁⲙⲧⲉ/ⲧⲙⲁⲥϩⲧⲟⲉ/ⲧⲙⲁⲍⲧ̄, and the twelve wisdoms). Sections 1223-1234 describing the operation of the fifth attribute (the feminine 'she' who reveals, seals, sends forth, nourishes, and makes new) are too fragmentary for confident filling; the verb ⲃⲉⲃⲉ 'gush forth' and ⲍⲱⲣⲡ-/ⲱⲗⲡ ⲁⲃⲁⲗ 'reveal' anchor the action but most short gaps lack constraint. Closing formula ϣⲁ ⲁⲛⲏⲍⲉ 'unto eternity' is intact. 26 gaps restored (mostly editor confirmations); 34 marked unrestorable, primarily in 1223-1234 where damage exceeds what spiritual structure alone can constrain.",
